# --- Database ---
database/churn.db
database/*.db
database/*.sqlite
database/*.sqlite3
*.db-journal

# --- Raw / large data ---
# `data/raw/telco_churn_raw.csv` IS tracked on purpose: it is the reproduction
# input for the whole pipeline, and `git check-ignore` must not claim otherwise.
# Its source, checksum and redistribution status are documented in
# docs/data_provenance.md. Everything else dropped into data/raw/ (Kaggle
# downloads, .xlsx workbooks, ad-hoc exports) stays out of Git.
#
# NOTE: the previous rules (`data/raw/*.csv`, `data/raw/`) ignored the tracked
# CSV and also made the `!data/raw/.gitkeep` negation inert — Git never descends
# into an ignored directory, so a negation below it cannot re-include a file.
data/raw/*
!data/raw/telco_churn_raw.csv

